        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-meet): align dtmf delay default",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Google Meet plugin metadata showed a shorter `voiceCall.dtmfDelayMs` default than the runtime and docs use, which could mislead setup and config surfaces that read defaults from the manifest.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis aligns the manifest default with the existing runtime default and locks the metadata value with a manifest test. It does not touch Google Meet runtime leave-call or Chrome transport behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and setup surfaces now see the same 12-second DTMF delay default that the Google Meet plugin actually applies at runtime.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts extensions/google-meet/src/config.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n",
